{Presiding: Committee Chair; Member for South Maafannu constituency, Abdulla Rifau}

Chair speaking:

In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Welcome to the 10th meeting of the People's Majlis Environment and Climate Change Committee. The meeting is being held in Committee Room 6. Today's date is 5 August 2026, Wednesday. The time is 1:20. We concluded the 9th meeting during the review of the Bill to amend Law No. 24/2022 (Waste Management Act), and decided to resume this meeting together with the Environment Ministry's comments, as we had not received those comments at that time. Now before us, and present at the meeting at this moment, are myself (Member for South Maafannu constituency, Abdulla Rifau), Member for Mulaku constituency Ibrahim Naufal, Member for Central Hulhumale' constituency Abdulla Shazeem, Member for Vilifushi constituency Hassan Waheed, and Member for North Hithadhoo constituency Abdulla Sodig. In the file in front of you, you will find a printout of the comments. We have received around 12 comments. The very first is a comment submitted on (p) of Article 8. What the Environment Ministry has requested to amend is the removal of (p) of Article 8 of the said Law. As the reason, they have stated that this article should be removed because formulating standards is a matter that falls within the responsibilities of the implementing agencies. And this article will be included in the responsibilities of the implementing agencies. (q) of Article 8. Removal of (q) of Article 8 of the said Law. As the reason, to remove this article because formulating these standards is a matter that falls within the responsibilities of the implementing agencies. And this article will be included in the responsibilities of the implementing agency. (r) of Article 8. Removal of (r) of Article 8 of the said Law. This article to be removed because formulating procedures is a matter that falls within the responsibilities of the implementing agencies. (s) - Establishing the waste management system, and making all regulations that need to be made to implement this Law. This is how this article already stands in the Law, this is how this article already stands in the Law. It is not considered necessary to amend this article. As the amendment included in the Bill is the formulation of standards, and since formulating standards is a matter that falls within the responsibilities of the implementing agencies, it is not considered necessary to amend this article. (t) of Article 8
